<h2 class="ds-section-title">Get started</h2>

<div class="ds-grid-2">
  <div class="ds-grid-content">
    <p class="ds-intro-text">
      DB Diff is built for the case a dump and compare cannot handle: a table with millions of rows where you need to
      know which rows drifted, without transferring the table.
    </p>

    <div class="ds-features-grid">
      <div class="ds-feature-card">
        <h3>Three engines</h3>
        <p>PostgreSQL, MySQL and ClickHouse, with one checksum contract across all three</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ds-feature-card">
        <h3>Checksums only</h3>
        <p>Server-side MD5 chunking, so only digests cross the wire when the tables match</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ds-feature-card">
        <h3>Pinpoint drift</h3>
        <p>A differing segment is read row by row and reported as primary keys</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ds-feature-card">
        <h3>Column control</h3>
        <p>Include or exclude columns to leave the noisy ones out of the comparison</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ds-feature-card">
        <h3>CI ready</h3>
        <p>Exit 0 when the tables match, 1 when they differ, 2 when the run failed</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ds-feature-card">
        <h3>Tunable segments</h3>
        <p>Trade query count against how much is read when something differs</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="ds-grid-terminal">
    <div class="ds-install-card">
      <h3>Install in one line</h3>
      <div class="ds-terminal__command">
        <span class="ds-terminal__prompt">$</span> go install matto.club/vetrina/db-diff@latest
      </div>
      <div class="ds-terminal__command">
        <span class="ds-terminal__prompt">$</span> brew tap clubmatto/vetrina https://github.com/clubmatto/vetrina &&
        brew install clubmatto/vetrina/db-diff
      </div>
      <p class="ds-install-note">Requires Go 1.24+ or Homebrew.</p>
    </div>
    <a href="https://github.com/clubmatto/vetrina/blob/main/db-diff/README.md" class="ds-btn-outline">Read the docs</a>
  </div>
</div>

<h2 class="ds-section-title">Requirements and limits</h2>

<div class="ds-callout">
  <div class="ds-limits">
    <p class="ds-intro-text">
      <strong>Engines:</strong> PostgreSQL 14 or newer, MySQL and ClickHouse. Both databases must run the same engine;
      cross engine comparison is DB Diff Pro.
    </p>
    <p class="ds-intro-text">
      <strong>Table:</strong> one integer primary key named <code>id</code>, with the same table name and column order
      on both sides.
    </p>
    <p class="ds-intro-text">
      <strong>Run:</strong> a differing segment is read whole, and the comparison is not a transaction. Pin the session
      timezone and charset on both connections.
    </p>
    <p class="ds-intro-text">
      <strong>License:</strong> MIT. The <a href="https://github.com/clubmatto/vetrina/releases">releases page</a>
      has the current version and checksums.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<h2 class="ds-section-title">Algorithm notes</h2>

<div class="ds-algo-notes">
  <p class="ds-algo-lede">
    DB Diff does the comparison inside the database. The wire carries checksums when the tables match, and rows only
    when they do not.
  </p>

  <ol class="ds-algo-steps">
    <li class="ds-algo-step">
      <span class="ds-algo-step-number">01</span>
      <h3 class="ds-algo-step-title">Segment the table</h3>
      <p class="ds-algo-step-text">
        The table is cut into ranges of primary keys, 10,000 by default. Both sides can address the same range without
        moving a row.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="ds-algo-step">
      <span class="ds-algo-step-number">02</span>
      <h3 class="ds-algo-step-title">Checksum each segment</h3>
      <p class="ds-algo-step-text">
        Each side hashes every compared column on its own, folds the digests with XOR, and returns one 64-bit checksum.
        Equal checksums skip the segment.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="ds-algo-step">
      <span class="ds-algo-step-number">03</span>
      <h3 class="ds-algo-step-title">Read only what differs</h3>
      <p class="ds-algo-step-text">
        A differing segment is read row by row and compared column by column. The output is the primary keys that
        changed.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <div class="ds-algo-code">
    <span class="ds-algo-code-label">Row checksum</span>
    <pre><code>md5( null_bitmap || md5(COALESCE(col_a, '')) || md5(COALESCE(col_b, '')) || ... ) -> first 8 bytes
segment = XOR(row checksums)</code></pre>
  </div>

  <div class="ds-algo-foot">
    <p class="ds-algo-note">
      The comparison runs within one engine. Engines render values their own way: a boolean is <code>true</code> in
      PostgreSQL and <code>1</code> in MySQL, so a cross engine run is refused rather than reported as every row
      changed. DB Diff Pro adds the canonical form that makes it possible.
    </p>
    <a
      href="https://github.com/clubmatto/vetrina/blob/main/db-diff/docs/how-it-works.md"
      class="ds-btn ds-btn--primary"
      >Read the full algorithm notes</a
    >
  </div>
</div>

